132	Create caches, `Ref`s and semaphores during acquisition, once per intended
133	Layer lifetime. A shared application Layer means shared state; a request Layer
134	means request state. Cache failure retention, size, timeout and concurrency
135	are deliberate policies, not universal defaults. Acquire external handles with
136	`Effect.acquireRelease` or the installed scoped constructor and keep release
137	inside that scope. Avoid closing a resource before a returned stream finishes.
