150	`Layer.provide` supplies a Layer's dependencies while exposing the target's
151	outputs. `Layer.provideMerge` also retains the supplied outputs for other
152	consumers. `Layer.mergeAll` combines independent Layers; it does not wire one
153	Layer's output into another's input. Share the same Layer value at the root so
154	normal build memoisation shares acquisition. Recreating a Layer factory or
155	building separate runtimes can create extra clients and separate state.
156	
157	Acquire individual dependency services, not the whole request Context. The
158	native host supplies request services in the incoming fibre; keep their lifetime
159	with that host. The separate TanStack frontend supplies client Layers without
160	borrowing the API request Context. Consumers import service contracts and
161	provide live Layers at the root, rather than importing raw SDK constructors.
162	
163	## Layer names
164	
165	Use:
166	
167	- `AccountsLive`;
168	- `AccountsMemory`;
169	- `AccountsTest` when it is test-specific;
170	- `AccountsHttpLive` only if multiple live transports coexist.
171	
172	`live.layer.ts` may export multiple closely related Layers, but avoid a global mega-Layer with unrelated domains.
173	
174	## Memory/test Layers
175	
176	Implement the identical service contract. A memory Layer may expose a separate control service for:
177	
178	- seeding state;
179	- observing calls;
180	- injecting failure;
181	- advancing a simulated provider state.
182	
183	Do not add testing-only methods to the Production service contract.
184	
185	Make state immutable/Effect-managed and tests scoped so suites cannot leak state.
186	
